{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/121872-wraith-vampire-are-ghouls-affected-by-the-fog","id":121872,"title":"Wraith/Vampire: Are Ghouls affected by the Fog?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-29T11:25:24-07:00","id":121872,"title":"Wraith/Vampire: Are Ghouls affected by the Fog?","content":"When a mortal is confronted with overtly supernatural displays of wraithly Arcanoi, his or her psyche weaves a Fog between itself and the phenomenon. States like amnesia, denial, panic and rage are all symptoms of a Fog touched human. However, some are not affected by the Fog: innocent children, animals, the insane and certain other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> I'm currently running a game where my players' ghouls just witnessed some pretty dramatic displays of Arcanoi. My question is: would the ghouls, who are in large part still mortal, suffer from the Fog, or would you say that the act of imbibing vitae has made them resistant to the Fog?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:25:13-07:00","id":121941,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to say yes, they would still suffer the Fog, but I'm not sure if the rules back me up. See if there's a ruling anywhere on Ghouls experiencing Lunacy and go with whatever that says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T13:51:25-07:00","id":121961,"title":"","content":"as the ghouls can suffer Delirium, as a thumb rule I say they suffer Fog, Mist and all the repertoire of supernatural curses...<br /> <br /> but, somewhere (probably on project twilight) they say a ghoul with 3 or more Discipline dots is enough supernatural and is thus fairly immune to Delirium; then I can say a ghoul with 3 or more Discipline dots (or 2 Discipline dots if you rule the Fog is less powerful than Delirium) is immune to the Fog, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border